      "html": "<p>Panaqolus albivermis received an official, valid name in 2013. It is one of the most beautiful L-numbers. Maximum length is around 10 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/l204_panaqolus_albivermis_en/",
      "html": "<p>The species originates from Peru.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/l204_panaqolus_albivermis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Some spotted individuals were stocked under the name L204a; however, they do not represent a different species. Even among captive bred specimens from wild collected, striped parents, spotted youngsters appear every now and then.</p>"
    }
